# Local developer secrets for the Gleanvolt.Worker app.
#
# Copy this file to ".env" (which is gitignored) and fill in real values. On startup the worker
# loads the nearest ".env" file into the process environment, so these reach the app whether it is
# started with `dotnet run` or the VS Code debugger. Real system/CI environment variables take
# precedence over anything set here.
#
# Keys use the ASP.NET Core convention: "__" (double underscore) separates configuration sections,
# so Solcast__ApiKey binds to the "Solcast:ApiKey" setting.

# Solcast API key (secret) -- get it from your Solcast account.
Solcast__ApiKey=your-solcast-api-key

# Optional: override non-secret Solcast settings here instead of appsettings.json if you prefer.
# Solcast__ResourceId=your-solcast-resource-id

# The weather comes from an external provider since #425, such as the OpenWeather plugin
# (plugins/Gleanvolt.Plugin.OpenWeather), which takes its own key. Gleanvolt needs none.

# Where this PV system is, and what it is made of. Non-secret, so appsettings.json could hold them,
# but it ships without a site: the inverter's address is required, and a development machine
# sets them (and its car, below) here. The values are examples.
#
# Pv__Id=home-roof
# Pv__Name=Home Roof
# Pv__Latitude=50.0755
# Pv__Longitude=14.4378
# Pv__Inverter__Host=192.168.1.10
# ChargeControl__Forecast__BatteryCapacityKWh=9.0
#
# Any of these can also be edited on the web UI's PV system page, which saves to
# src/Gleanvolt.Worker/data/pv-system.json (Pv__OverridesPath) under `dotnet run`. A value there wins
# over this file until it is reverted on that page or the file is deleted.
#
# The car, also optional (the web UI's Car page edits the same keys):
#
# Ev__Vehicles__0__Id=my-car
# Ev__Vehicles__0__Name=My car
# Ev__Vehicles__0__BatteryCapacityKWh=77
# Ev__Vehicles__0__Phases=3
#
# Retired: Weather__Latitude, Weather__Longitude, Solax__Inverter__*, Solax__EvCharger__* and
# Solax__PollIntervalSeconds. Setting any of them now stops the worker at startup with a message
# naming its replacement -- being quietly pointed at a default device is the failure that refusal
# exists to prevent.

# The car's battery level comes from a car plugin (gleanvolt-cars) since #477: Gleanvolt reads no car itself.
# Choose "A plugin" on the Car page and run the plugin beside the worker; it keeps the car's account on its
# own page.
